.SS Abstract
This keyword must only be used with \f[B]global\f[R] or
\f[CR]static\f[R] variables when needed.
.PP
It marks the variable as \f[B]thread\-local\f[R], meaning \f[B]each
thread gets its own separate instance\f[R] of that variable.
.PP
This ensures the variable is \f[B]not shared between threads\f[R],
preventing race conditions or unintended data sharing.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]extern\f[R] local int g_variable;
\f[I]//     \(ha\(ha\(ha\(ha\(ha\f[R]
.EE
.PP
Add that if you\(aqre trying to access your global variable using the
\f[CR]extern\f[R] keyword.
.SS Side Notes
Yes, you must use the \f[CR]local\f[R] keyword in the \f[B]prototypes of
global variables\f[R] too.
